# Licenses and bundled driver inventory

This file reconciles the OCI image license label of the FSDK OCI image
`ghcr.io/projectbluefin/ps-printer-app` with the third-party print drivers and
libraries bundled into it. See "## LEGAL STUFF" in `README.md` for the short
form.

## OCI license label scope

`elements/oci/ps-printer-app.bst` sets the image config label

    org.opencontainers.image.licenses=Apache-2.0

and `.github/workflows/registry-actions.yml` puts the same value on the
published index as the `org.opencontainers.image.licenses` annotation.
(`rockcraft.yaml` also declares `license: Apache-2.0`, but it is an upstream
reference file and builds nothing this fork ships.)

This label describes **only the ps-printer-app application source** in this
repository, which is Apache-2.0 (`LICENSE`): `ps-printer-app.c` and the files
`elements/printer-app/application.bst` builds from it, and the entrypoint
installed by `elements/printer-app/runtime-files.bst`. It does **not** describe
the third-party print drivers, PostScript PPD files and printing stack that are
also in the image.

The label value is intentionally left as `Apache-2.0`. Changing it to a GPL
expression would mislead consumers the other way, because the application
source is genuinely Apache-2.0, and the image as a whole has no single license
expression (see below). The label's intended scope is clarified here and in the
README: it covers the application source, not the bundled components.

