These transitive components are **not** covered by the `Apache-2.0` OCI
label. Do not read `org.opencontainers.image.licenses=Apache-2.0` as a
statement about their licenses.

## Mixed / unresolved files

The build copies the PPDs unmodified: at the pinned refs the `*CloseUI` and
`*1284DeviceId` header fixups in `hplip-ps.bst` and `foomatic-ps-ppds.bst`
match no file, and every PPD in the two archives of a local x86_64 build is
byte-identical to its upstream file. Each PPD therefore keeps its own header
notice. Counting those notices (a text scan of each file's `*%` comments, not a
legal review):

- HPLIP `prnt/ps` (520): 455 carry the MIT notice; 40 carry the MIT notice
  plus a "redistribution ... as long as ... the contents of the file is not
  altered" condition; 13 carry only that redistribution condition (for
  example `hp-designjet_t1500-postscript.ppd`); 12 carry no copyright or
  license notice (for example `hp-designjet_t1530-postscript.ppd`).
  `debian/copyright` covers them only through its `Files: *` GPL-2+ stanza.
- Foomatic-db `db/source/PPD` selection (4,026): 3,030 carry the MIT notice;
  481 carry the MIT notice plus a "not altered" redistribution condition
  (Epson, HP, Kyocera, Utax); 345 carry a GNU GPL version 2 notice, 238 of
  them "or any later version" (Brother, KONICA_MINOLTA, Oki, Sharp, Toshiba,
  one Oce); 170 carry a BSD-style notice (Lexmark).

These files are recorded as mixed-license rather than collapsed into one
expression. The PPDs with an added "not altered" condition or no notice at
all, and the `hpps` psutils-derived sources, are unresolved and need a
maintainer decision before the label or any SPDX license field names them.

The README says the application is Apache-2.0 "with an exception to allow
linking against GPL2/LGPL2 software", but this repository's `LICENSE` and
`NOTICE` do not contain that exception's text; that is also unresolved.

## SBOM

`just sbom` (see `Justfile`) runs buildstream-sbom on
`oci/ps-printer-app.bst --deps all` and writes `ps-printer-app.spdx.json`: one
SPDX package per BuildStream element and per source, with its download location
and version or ref. It runs without `--with-licenses`, and the elements declare
no license provenance, so the SBOM has no license fields. It is the component
inventory (including build-only elements), not a license inventory: the license
terms are the ones in this file.

Only `.github/workflows/registry-actions.yml` publishes the SBOM: on each push
to `testing` it runs `just sbom`, attaches the SPDX file to the image index and
signs it with keyless cosign. Nothing has been published yet, so no signed SBOM
exists; publishing is held until the PPD-upload security sign-off
(`projectbluefin/ps-printer-app#45`).

## Verification (not done in this audit)

The source-level trace above is based on the pinned upstream sources named in
the elements. Verifying the licenses actually present in the built image and in
the signed SBOM on both release architectures (amd64 and arm64) must be done at
release time, from the published OCI image and its SBOM, not by inspecting this
repository. See `projectbluefin/ps-printer-app#27` for the security sign-off
that gates public promotion.
